  "summary": "Retain combined-axillary-relief-v11 (5a64c10f-e861-4957-9d6d-1d718fe6a3b1) as an unqualified bilateral shoulder axillary relief and hip deformation diagnostic only. Method v11 inherits bilateral shoulder proximal-arm section handles and dual-plane hip retraction field with expanded 0.045H (45.1mm) support radius, and applies a targeted -15mm posterior Y-offset on the Right armpit (c_chest[1] -= (15.0 / 1000.0)) to address the persistent deep fold self-intersection at 60\u00b0 shoulder adduction. Straight Right UpperArm 60\u00b0 drops to EXACT ZERO CONTACTS (390 baseline -> 44 -> 14 -> 12 -> 0), and compound UpperArmR 60\u00b0 twist 20 drops to EXACT ZERO CONTACTS (386 baseline -> 0). BOTH straight 60\u00b0 shoulders (Left 348->0, Right 390->0), BOTH straight 90\u00b0 shoulders (Left 93->0, Right 166->0), compound UpperArmL 60\u00b0 twist -20 (363->0), compound UpperArmR 60\u00b0 twist 20 (386->0), and all three persistent hip self-intersection poses (10: 42->0, 22: 17->0, 23: 42->0) now simultaneously achieve ZERO contacts. Across all 25 evaluated poses, there are ZERO contact regressions, ZERO seam openings, condition number <= 10 (1.172 on shoulders, 1.425 on hips), and all displacements strictly respect frozen caps (hips max posed 0.00819H / cap 0.03H, max rest 0.01159H / cap 0.04H; shoulders max posed 0.01800H / cap 0.02H, max rest 0.01898H / cap 0.02H). Bilateral morph normal delta transport on all four shoulder targets eliminates active support normal divergence on training poses to < 0.000019\u00b0 with 0 support vertices worse over 1\u00b0, passes Khronos gltf-validator with 0 errors, and verifies Babylon GPU shader defines (BONETEXTURE, MORPHTARGETS_NORMAL, NUM_BONE_INFLUENCERS 8, NUM_MORPH_INFLUENCERS 7, NONUNIFORMSCALING absent). All assets remain unqualified diagnostic evidence only.",
